- One token per word, in text order, covering every English word. Skip punctuation and emoji; "surface" must be copied
  EXACTLY from the text, case kept, without punctuation ("Hi!" → Hi, "Name?" → Name).
- Contractions are one token: I'm (lemma "I am", pos pronoun), don't (lemma "do not", pos verb), Where's (lemma "where is").
- Phrasal verbs, idioms and set expressions are ONE token: ran into (lemma "run into", pos phrasal_verb),
  in a hurry (pos phrase), flat white (pos noun) — only real set expressions, not any two words.
- Fields: surface, lemma, pos, translation, lemma_translation, cefr, note.
  - lemma: dictionary form, lowercase except proper nouns and "I" (is → be, ran → run, cups → cup, Della → Della).
  - pos: noun | verb | adjective | adverb | pronoun | preposition | conjunction | interjection | determiner | numeral |
    phrasal_verb | idiom | phrase.
  - translation: <%= native.name %> meaning in THIS sentence, short, in the form that fits the <%= native.name %> translation.
    lemma_translation: dictionary meaning of the lemma in <%= native.name %> (omit if the same).
  - cefr: A1–C1 estimate of the lemma.
  - note: ONLY for target words, phrasal verbs, idioms and tricky grammar: one short <%= native.name %> sentence.
- No romanization, breakdown or politeness fields.

